---
import Section from './Section.astro';
---

<Section labelledby="why-title">
  {/* The script face carries this section instead of the display face — it is
      the ad's sell line, and the one place on the page where the argument, not
      a label, is the heading. It was running at the size of a hero aside; at
      full strength it becomes the section's peak. Narrower measure so it
      breaks into two lines and reads as a statement rather than a caption. */}
  <h2
    id="why-title"
    class="neon max-w-[18ch] font-script text-4xl text-balance [--tube:var(--color-signal)] sm:max-w-[22ch] sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
  >
    a fresh challenge in hardware
  </h2>

  {/* A tube rule signs off the quote, where a default 2px border used to
      separate it from the copy. Kept short so it reads as an underline rather
      than repeating the full-width track in "how it works". */}
  <span
    class="neon-rule mt-8 block h-1 w-full max-w-sm"
    style="--tube: var(--color-signal)"
    aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div
    class="mt-8 text-base text-pretty text-phosphor-dim sm:columns-2 sm:gap-col"
  >
    <p>
      Mint is intended to be a refreshing break from the high-stress long-term
      projects that many teens spend all their time on.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Despite being a lower time requirement and lower complexity challenge, it
      still maintains flexibility for both beginners and advanced users alike.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
